  "origin": "Danish instruction-following pairs derived from Danish Wikipedia, where prompts ask for a short encyclopedic article and the target is the corresponding Wikipedia text. The underlying Danish Wikipedia content is licensed CC-BY-SA 4.0 (Wikimedia). A same-named sub-source (190.21M tokens, license listed as Unknown) also appears inside the dfm-dyna-instruct collection; the standalone synquid/wiki-instruct-da dataset is the larger, separately-versioned release. Form: reformatted. Contributed 988M sampled tokens per epoch to the DFM Mimir v1 corpus (1.40%). Note: the dataset repository is gated (contact-information access agreement required on Hugging Face); the license field here reflects the underlying Wikipedia text, not a dataset-level license declared by the publisher.",
